rs like william  striker for example in marvel comics  he's a religious evangelical  fundamentalist who believes  it's his mission from god to kill  mutants so he created the purifiers he  has no powers whatsoever but he is  exceedingly charismatic and that's what  makes him so intriguing magneto  speaks for himself but you see this kind  of stuff all the time  and i feel like sony launching  villain-based films  movies that focus on the stories of the  villains is  great it's a great idea craven the  hunter can be cool sometimes  i guess it really depends on what  particular story that you're reading if  you do read the story where he basically  eats a whole bunch of spiders to try to  give himself spider-man's powers because  he's crazy  as a little wonky but if you read craven  the hunter stories that are akin to like  the most dangerous game right the idea  of the hunter hunting people  then you can get some really really cool  stories out of it you can get a lot of  depth to his character the idea of the  chameleon appearing it's cool  because a chameleon can just become  anybody write a master of disguise a lot  of these villains that are being built  up i feel like are going to play a much  bigger role as far as what sony wants to  do with spider-man but i think it's a  genius idea so i don't really have any  hate for it having said that  chameleons has long since deserved a  role as far as movies go he was the  first villain peter parker ever fought  so i'm kind of surprised that we haven't  really seen a chameleon-centric film up  to this point  i mean a lot of people might say well i  mean you know it's chameleon right how  could you possibly make them interesting  people said the same thing about iron  man and look at we are as far as the  iron man films go so  you can't really write them off at the  end of the day it all comes down to how  the character is written so  i am excited to see the chameleon might  appear in craven i would much rather see  a solo chameleon film depending on how  it's done but at the end of the day  it is a cool thing that we're getting  there so i can't be too upset about it  so our next little bit of news here and  not a whole lot to talk about here  aquaman 2 is officially titled aquaman  and the lost kingdom it may be  that it ties into a lot of the dc  rebirth stuff so it kind of gives us  like the kings of  old and all that kind of stuff but the  first aquaman film was a little too  fast and the furious for me in terms of  how it was shot and how it felt having  said that it was still good  but i don't want to be one of these guys  who's just like everything sucked  it was still a pretty good movie it was  certainly one of the best films that dc  had released in a long long time  but i am excited to see what this does  turn into one of the funny things about  aquaman there's a lot of history and a  lot of mythos there right there's a lot  of stuff that goes on with the  characters so  if they tell it right they can really  give us a lot of the old  stories with regards to like aquaman  arthur curry and a lot of the history  that goes in there and all that kind of  stuff so  i'm down right at the very least it's  kind of cool to see that he got a name  but you know i don't really know what  significance that has on the nature  of the story right maybe just one of  those lost kingdoms that exist out there  that are not officially part of atlantis  but they just kind of exist out there  as kind of a side along to atlantis and  sort of do their own thing  again we're not entirely sure here but  another cool little thing that we saw  we got to see kamala khan using her  powers on set well i mean when i say  using her power is really more of her  just moving like she will use her powers  she's just pushing right there's not  really a whole lot going on there it's  really just kind of like the set pieces  but it is kind of cool kamala khan is  one of these characters where i'm  interested to see what they do with her  because there really is no middle ground  when it comes to kamala khan either you  love her or you hate her and a lot of  that is predicated on your ability to  identify with her  given the nature of her religion that is  very much rooted in tradition family  values but when you're living in the  states  family values kind of exist sometimes  in movies but we're not nearly as family  oriented as a lot of people in the  middle east  and so when you have that traditional  culture clashing with a lot of the  progressive cultural ideas that exist  here in the states  especially when you're a teenager trying  to fit in that can resonate a lot with a  lot of younger kids  but i imagine it can only really  resonate strongly if you can identify  with her character  having said that i'm not calling her a  lost cause one of the best decisions  that marvel ever made was putting her on  the champions which were basically the  young avengers but by like  a different name but it was still a cool  concept seeing her team up with sam  alexander nova and miles morales  spider-man i don't know if any s that's  really gonna happen but the point that  i'm making here is your ability to enjoy  kamala khan  is not really relegated to whether or  not you can identify with her being  a muslim pakistani american trying to  fit into american culture while  respecting her roots as far as being a  muslim from pakistan  i'm sure they'll make a lot of cool  jokes and they'll be like the young  angsty teenager vibe and so there'll be  a lot of cool moments in there that i'm  sure that you'll enjoy but i think to  really grasp the character you kind of  have to really be able to understand  where she's coming from but  you know at the end of the day i'm  excited to see it i love watching like  teenage superheroes  because there's just so much youth and  vibrance that's thrown in there  plus they're funny right like sam  alexander is nova is hilarious  he's a lot cooler than richard ryder was  richard ryder was boring as hell  i know i read him for 20 years  but moving on to our next topic and this  is probably one of the most significant  things  that we've heard of recently which  actually came out maybe about 20 hours  ago about yesterday as far as the marvel  cinematic universe what if series and  again  this is just a bit of a rumor here eric  killmonger and robert downey jr's iron  man  are supposed to team up what an odd  couple  but how awesome would that be  i loved the character of eric killmonger  i loved him in the movies  the only thing i didn't like about his  appearance in the movies is that in the  comics he defeated black panther  even when black panther had his powers  and that was designed to be a testament  to how  capable eric killmonger was i kind of  wish they'd carry that over to the  movies that eric killmonger defeated  t'challa even when t'challa had his  powers but i think they kind of had to  mix that out so they could basically  have the two of them fight on a more  even keel  when they both had the heart-shaped herb  at the end of the film but regardless of  the circumstance  i loved it right i loved eric killmonger  michael b  jordan is is probably one of my top  three favorite actors throughout  all of hollywood i've been following him  since the wire for those of you guys  remember how long he's been acting but  to see him and robert downey jr's iron  man team  up in the what if series which may or  may not be voiced by robert downey jr  sounds awesome man because those are two  characters who never met and i kind of  always wanted them to  there wouldn't really be a reason for  them to there wouldn't really be a  reason for like  you know iron man to show up in wakanda  and face off against eric killmonger  alongside black panther that'd be  something that you'd see if eric  killmonger had survived black panther  one and then became maybe a more  formidable villain or appeared in like a  different film  or something like that if we saw  something akin to like acts of vengeance  where loki gathered together  all these different villains and then  had them face off against all the heroes  but switched around who was facing off  against who so like red skull would  fight hawkeye  and like eric killmonger would fight  iron man and then maybe something else  would go on crossbones might fight black  panther i don't really know but at the  end of the day kind of switching them  around  that would have been a cool thing to see  but even if we're only going to see it  in in the form of an animated series  i'm excited for it man these two guys  meeting i can't be the only one  right i can't be the only one who's  excited at the idea of eric killmonger  encountering iron man right i'm sure you  guys are hyped for that too but  having said that guys this wraps up our  episode of the rumor roundup  let us know in the comments if there's  any important news bits that you think  we missed and we'll include those in  next week's video and i will catch you  all later  peace
 

